{"name":"Spring Branch","hex":"#a98c37","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spring","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move or burst forth.","To appear."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of springing: a leap, a jump.","The season of the year in temperate regions in which temperatures and daylight hours rise, and plants spring from the ground and into bloom and dormant animals spring to life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spring"},{"term":"branch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The woody part of a tree arising from the trunk and usually dividing.","Any of the parts of something that divides like the branch of a tree."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To arise from the trunk or a larger branch of a tree.","To produce branches."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/branch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spring (hydrology)","blocks":[{"text":"A spring is a natural exit point at which groundwater emerges from an aquifer and flows across the ground surface as surface water. It is a component of the hydrosphere, as well as a part of the water cycle. Springs have long been important for humans as a source of fresh water, especially in arid regions which have relatively little annual rainfall."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Big_Spring_Missouri_1-02Aug08.jpg/330px-Big_Spring_Missouri_1-02Aug08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_(hydrology)"},{"title":"Spring Branch (Murderkill River tributary)","blocks":[{"text":"Spring Branch is a 2.63 mi (4.23 km) long 1st order tributary to the Murderkill River in Kent County, Delaware."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_Branch_(Murderkill_River_tributary)"},{"title":"Branch","blocks":[{"text":"A branch, also called a ramus in botany, is a stem that grows off from another stem, or when structures like veins in leaves are divide